      "narrative": "Little Giant, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. CIMT (NW Team 13). CIMT is also managing the Sisi incident. Thirty miles northwest of Leavenworth, WA. Timber and dormant brush. Minimal fire behavior with creeping, backing and smoldering. Structures threatened. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Precipitation occurred over the fire area yesterday. Sisi, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. Ten miles northwest of Stehekin, WA. Closed timber litter and timber. Moderate fire behavior with backing, flanking and creeping. Residences threatened. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Precipitation occurred over the fire area yesterday. Austin, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. CIMT (CA Team 2). CIMT is also managing The Narrows and Grasshopper incidents. Twenty-five miles southeast of Estacada, OR. Brush, timber and closed timber litter. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering and creeping. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Precipitation occurred over the fire area yesterday. The Narrows, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. Fifteen miles southeast of Estacada, OR. Grass, brush and light slash. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Precipitation occurred over the fire area yesterday. Grasshopper, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. Fourteen miles southwest of Dufur, OR. Brush, hardwood litter and closed timber litter. Minimal fire behavior with creeping and smoldering. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Precipitation occurred over the fire area yesterday. Hagen, Umatilla NF, USFS. Transfer of command from CIMT (NW Team 7) back to the local unit will occur tomorrow. Twenty-six miles east of Pendleton, OR. Timber. Minimal fire behavior with creeping and smoldering. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Three Queens, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. Six miles east of Snoqualmie Pass, WA. Timber, brush and grass. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering. Numerous residences and critical infrastructure threatened. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Sinlahekin, Northeast Region, Washington DNR. One mile west of Tonasket, WA. Timber, brush and grass. Minimal fire behavior with creeping and smoldering. Area, road and trail closures in effect. * Second Street, Washington State Fire Marshal's Office. One mile southeast of Benton City, WA. Grass and brush. Extreme fire behavior with wind-driven runs and running. Residences and energy infrastructure threatened."
